  "final_message": "Wait, I have launched the command and will wait for it to finish.\nRunning tests in the background, waiting for completion...\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n1. **Breaking Change for External Consumers**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is consumed by downstream services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` directly would break deployed consumers expecting the field in schema version 3.\n2. **Domain Model Dependency**: The [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model supplies the data used by [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) to construct the published event. Removing it from the model would break the event publisher.\n\n### Recommended Approach:\nPer **ARCH-4**, any removal must follow a deprecation cycle:\n- Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n- Coordinate with `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` teams to ensure they have stopped consuming the field.\n- Remove the field in a subsequent schema version bump once consumers have migrated.\n",
